t_names/148"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Lightweight (≤60 kilograms), Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "11 – 23 October 1964"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/448"} "Korakuen Horu, Bunkyo, Tokyo"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/23419"} "34 from 34 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Single elimination tournament."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/7728"} "Józef Grudzień"] " of Poland had made his major championships début at the 1963 European Championships but had been dispatched at the quarter-final stage by [Janos Kajdi] of Hungary who would take the title. Kajdi fell at the equivalent stage at Tokyo to " [:a {:href "/athletes/8483"} "Vilikton Barannikov"] " of the Soviet Union and this opened up the possibility of a Polish title win. The final between Grudzień and Barannikov was closely fought but the Russian, the more aggressive of the two, was continually backed up by the left jab of the Pole, who won a unanimous decision. Grudzień won the European championships in 1967 and returned to the Olympic Games in 1968 where he lost against " [:a {:href "/athletes/8688"} "Ronnie Harris"] " in the final.  Coincidentally he beat a different " [:a {:href "/athletes/8687"} "Ronnie Harris"] " in the semi-final in Tokyo."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/7728"} "Józef Grudzień"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/POL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/POL.png"}] "POL"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [: